  narrator: 0
  playerThoughts: 0
  lines:
  - speaker: 0
    kind: 2
    text: 'You stand there in silence for quite a while, brain struggling to comprehend
      what you just learned. It has never occurred to you that Bradley may have his
      own problems. He always seemed like a guy who treats other people like dirt
      just because he can, purely out of enjoyment for being an asshole. Never once
      did you think that maybe it was some sort of fucked up coping mechanism for
      the shit going on in his own life. '
    videoEventId: 
  - speaker: 0
    kind: 2
    text: Not that it made any difference. Even with his own life being shit, that
      still gives him no right to make everyone else a victim of his misery. Though
      you can at least somewhat understand his process of thinking, you still resent
      him deeply. Maybe even more than before.
    videoEventId: 
  - speaker: 0
    kind: 2
    text: "The more you try to calm down, the more you spiral. So, all you had to
      endure was just because Bradley couldn\u2019t get help like every other normal
      fucking human being?? Just because his home was shit, you and others were humiliated
      and pushed down time and time again in a sick attempt to regain control of
      his stupid life?? "
    videoEventId: 
  - speaker: 0
    kind: 2
    text: 'A thundering headache was beginning to build behind your eyes, your stomach
      rolling with nausea from how intense your emotions are. A thunderous noise
      abruptly snaps you out of your rage, a few books had fallen off the desk and
      slammed onto the ground. '
    videoEventId: 
  - speaker: 0
    kind: 2
    text: "Right. The ghost. You could cry angrily later, for now you have priorities
      to sort out. At least this sign of life from the ghost could be taken as a
      sign that you were on the right track, that your deduction of suicide due to
      Bradley\u2019s bullying had something to back it up. You wipe the tears \u2013
      you hadn\u2019t even noticed you started crying \u2013 from your cheeks and
      march to your own dorm. It was time to put an end to this tomorrow, to finally
      let this poor soul rest in peace. "
    videoEventId: 
